      "side": 1,
      "message": "The dispatcher declares this name but HTTPScheme installs the handler, in two addAfter() chains, so the \"aggregator sits right after me\" invariant is maintained by hand elsewhere and a mistake degrades to one LOG.error per message with the aggregated path still green. Would it be cleaner for the dispatcher to take maxRequestBodySize and install the aggregator itself in handlerAdded? That makes AGGREGATOR_NAME private and retires isDownstreamOf, the error branch, and the new ordering test.",
