      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T14:59:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This resolves the aggregator per message, and isDownstreamOf then allocates the full pipeline name list and scans it twice. So a 100 MB chunked upload pays roughly three pipeline traversals and one throwaway list per 8 KB chunk on the event loop, to re-derive something that CANNOT CHANGE during a request. Right? \n\nCould startRequest() resolve the context once, do the ordering check there, and keep it in a field beside mode for forward to use?",
      "revId": "6ff0a561f35bf5f20bee591a31b9f4adde35b99f",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
